Try to do: b <your cd drive> -flags A
The aboot won't try to autoboot any configurations and you should get 
into aboot prompt.
 From there you could use "help" to get list of supported command.
l - display preconfigured boot configurations (one of them)
To boot preconfigured boot configuration just enter its number and press 
Enter. :)
You could try rescue boot configuration just to check out that kernel 
could be booted and all your hardware is recognized.
If it does - reboot and choose one of the "text" or "graphic" install modes.

